fuxi: 0132 -- let IOKit quiesce (the busy hold that was never released)

Port of upstream topaz 0128 to FUXI, which never got it: that fix is gated on
ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET and this board is FUXI.

StartIOKitMatching() takes a registry-root busy count if OSKext::iokitDaemonAvailable(),
to be released when the IOKit daemon reports that it launched.  On this board there is no
kext daemon to launch, so nothing ever reports, nothing ever releases the count, and the
registry root stays busy forever.  IOKit therefore never quiesces, configd's
InterfaceNamer never says "quiet", and every daemon that waits for that -- SpringBoard
included -- waits at boot.  Upstream's note is "wifid hung boot"; on this port it is the
plateau at 17% where launchd is up and nothing else happens for minutes.

FUXI takes no hold and releases none.

Harness: applied=131 skipped=0.
